  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"By repurposing well-known and rare Soviet posters, "Solaris" attempts to evoke a very specific and simple metaphor: that among the many false representations of his failed revolution, Lenin promised the sun and everything under it -- and delivered nothing ... For "Solaris," the central idea of the sun and its rays shining on nothing is the crux of the series"-- Pages 2-3.</subfield>
